During the run-off, Landrieu was out-spent three-to-one by Republican contender [[Suzanne Haik Terrell]], the Louisiana Elections Commissioner. Terrell also had prominent Republicans including President [[George W. Bush]] and Vice President [[Dick Cheney]] visit Louisiana to campaign on her behalf. Republicans, confident of victory having gained seats in the elections [[2002 United States House of Representatives elections|to the House of Representatives]] and to the Senate, solidifying control of the former and taking control of the latter, publicly called the election "Operation Icing on the Cake".<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.msmagazine.com/news/uswirestory.asp?id=7327|title=Landrieu Faces Terrell for Senate in Louisiana Runoff Race|date=December 6, 2002|website=[[Ms. (magazine)|Ms.]]|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20021220100208/http://www.msmagazine.com/news/uswirestory.asp?id=7327|archive-date=December 20, 2002}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|url=https://prospect.org/article/reversal-fortune/|title=Reversal of Fortune|last=Stevens|first=Allison|date=December 12, 2012|website=[[The American Prospect]]|url-status=live|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181105194122/https://prospect.org/article/reversal-fortune/|archive-date=November 5, 2018}}</ref> Some Democrats{{Who|date=October 2019}} responded by calling their efforts "Operation Wipe that Smirk off of Bush's Face"<ref>[http://www.dailykos.net/archives/000654.html More thoughts on Louisiana victories] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160304070047/http://www.dailykos.net/archives/000654.html |date=March 4, 2016 }} Daily Kos, December 8, 2002</ref> and dubbed Landrieu's subsequent narrow run-off victory, "Operation Pie in the Face".<ref>[http://www.dailykos.net/archives/000653.html Operation "Pie in the Face": Dems sweep LA] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160304102227/http://www.dailykos.net/archives/000653.html |date=March 4, 2016 }} Daily Kos, December 8, 2002</ref>

